u=0.311,pos=0.189,compound=0.3635"],[["neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=Principles"],["Principles"],[["Principles","NOUN","principle","",["ROOT","principle"]]],"neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0"],[["neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=8.","neg=0.032,neu=0.909,pos=0.059,compound=0.3182,span=Our digital cooperation will be guided by the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations and the following cross-cutting and mutually reinforcing principles: The inclusive participation of all States and other stakeholders is the cornerstone of this Compact.","neg=0.0,neu=0.0,pos=0.0,compound=0.0,span=Our cooperation will close the digital divides within and between States and advance an equitable digital environment for all; This Compact is development-oriented and rooted in the 2030 Agenda.","neg=0.273,neu=0.612,pos=0.114,compound=-0.4404,span=Our cooperation will harness technologies to fast-track progress, eradicate poverty and leave no one behind.","neg=0.0,neu=0.939,pos=0.061,compound=0.34,span=This includes targeted efforts to address the needs of developing countries, in particular the least developed countries, landlocked developing countries and small island developing States, as well as the specific challenges facing middle-income countries; This Compact is anchored in international law, including international human rights law.","neg=0.039,neu=0.675,pos=0.286,compound=0.8591,span=All human rights, including civil, political, economic, social and cultural rights, and fundamental freedoms, must be respected, protected and promoted online and offline.","neg=0.0,neu=0.966,pos=0.034,compound=0.3182,span=Our cooperation will harness digital technologies to advance all human rights, including the rights of the child, the rights of persons with disabilities and the right to development; Gender equality and the empowerment of all women and girls and their full, equal and meaningful participation in the digital space are essential to close the gender digital divide and advance sustainable development.","neg=0.12,neu=0.793,pos=0.087,compound=-0.5106,span=Our cooperation will empower all women and girls, encourage leadership of women, mainstream a gender perspective and counter and eliminate all forms of violence, including sexual and gender-based violence that occurs through or is amplified by the use of technology; Digital technologies unlock new capabilities and opportunities for advancing environmental sustainability.","neg=0.097,neu=0.842,pos=0.061,compound=-0.34,span=Our cooperation will leverage digital technologies for sustainability while minimizing their negative environmental impacts; Equitable and meaningful inclusion in the digital economy requires tackling existing concentrations of technological capacity and market power.","neg=0.0,neu=0.907,pos=0.093,compound=0.6369,span=Our cooperation will aim to ensure that the benefits of digital cooperation are fairly distributed and do not exacerbate existing inequalities or impede the full achievement of sustainable development; Accessible and affordable data and digital technologies and services are essential to enable every person to participate fully in the digital world.","neg=0.065,neu=0.787,pos=0.149,compound=0.4588,span=Our cooperation will promote digital accessibility for all and support linguistic and cultural diversity in the digital space; Digital systems that communicate and exchange are critical catalysts for development.","neg=0.0,neu=0.649,pos=0.351,compound=0.9274,span=Our cooperation will advance interoperability between digital systems and compatible governance approaches; Safe, secure and trustworthy emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence, offer new opportunities to turbocharge development.","neg=0.0,neu=0.886,pos=0.114,compound=0.7906,span=Our cooperation will advance a responsible, accountable, transparent and human-centric approach to the life cycle of digital and emerging technologies, which includes the pre-design, design, development, evaluation, testing, deployment, use, sale, procurement, operation and decommissioning stages, with effective human oversight; Creativity and competition drive digital advances.","neg=0.0,neu=0.838,pos=0.162,compound=0.9062,span=Our cooperation will foster innovation and the potential for societies and businesses, regardless of size or origin, to reap the benefits of digitalization and thrive in the digital economy; Governments, the private sector, civil society, the technical community, academia and international and regional organizations, in their respective roles and responsibilities, are essential to advance an inclusive, open, safe and secure digital future.","neg=0.0,neu=0.925,pos=0.075,compound=0.5719,span=Our cooperation will be multi-stakeholder and harness the contributions of all; We will enhance partnerships to ensure the provision of the required means of implementation to developing countries, including the mobilization of financial resources, capacity-building and the transfer of technology on mutually agreed terms; The digital world is evolving at pace.","neg=0.05,neu=0.793,pos=0.156,compound=0.5267,span=Our cooperation must be forward- looking and capable of identifying, anticipating, assessing, monitoring and adapting to emerging technologies so that we can seize opportunities and respond to new and emerging risks and challenges."],["Our digital cooperation","the purposes","principles","the Charter","the United Nations","-","mutually reinforcing principles","The inclusive participation","all States","other stakeholders","the cornerstone","this Compact","Our cooperation","the digital divides","States","an equitable digital environment","all","This Compact","the 2030 Agenda","Our cooperation","technologies","fast-track progress","poverty","no one","This","targeted efforts","the needs","developing countries","in particular the least developed countries","developing countries","small island","States","the specific challen