 child safety policies and standards, in compliance with international human rights law, including the Convention on the Rights of the Child (SDGs 3, 5 and 10); Establish regular collaboration between national online safety institutions to exchange best practices and develop shared understandings of actions to protect privacy, freedom of expression and access to information while addressing harms (SDG 17); Ensure that laws and regulations on the use of technology in areas such as surveillance and encryption are in compliance with international law ( SDGs 10 and 16); Develop, in consultation with all relevant stakeholders, effective methodologies to measure, monitor and counter all forms of violence and abuse in the digital space (SDGs 5 and 16); Monitor and review digital platform policies and practices on countering child sexual exploitation and abuse which occurs through or is amplified by the use of technology, including distribution over digital platforms of child sexual abuse or child sexual exploitation material, as well as solicitation or grooming for the purpose of committing a sexual offence against a child (SDG 3).","idx":43,"match_words":["commit","create","a safe and secure online space","user","ensure","their mental health","well","being","common","standard","industry","action","compliance","international law","promote","safe","space","address content","digital","platform","harm","individual","take","account work","way","united","nations","entity","regional","organization","multi","stakeholder","initiative","sdgs","the development","implementation","national","online","child","safety","policy","standard","compliance","international","human","right","law","include","the convention","the rights","the child","sdgs","establish","regular collaboration","national","online","safety","exchange","good","practice","develop","share","understanding","action","protect","privacy","freedom","access","information","address","harm","sdg","ensure","law","the use","techno