a platforms to enhance the transparency and accountability of their systems, including terms of service, content moderation and recommendation algorithms and handling of users' personal data in local languages, to empower users to make informed choices and provide or withdraw informed consent (SDGs 9 and 10); Call on social media platforms to provide researchers access to data, with safeguards for user privacy, to ensure transparency and accountability to build an evidence base on how to address misinformation and disinformation and hate speech that can inform government and industry policies, standards and best practices (SDGs 9, 16 and 17); Call on digital technology companies and developers to continue to develop solutions and publicly communicate actions to counter potential harms, including hate speech and discrimination, from artificial intelligence-enabled content.Such measures include incorporation of safeguards into artificial intelligence model training processes, identification of artificial intelligence-generated material, authenticity certification for content and origins, labelling, watermarking and other techniques (SDGs 10, 16 and 17).","idx":48,"match_words":["far","urgently","call","digital","technology","company","social","medium","platform","enhance","the transparency","accountability","system","include","term","service","content moderation","recommendation","user","datum","local","language","empower","user","make","provide","informed consent","sdgs","call","social","medium","platform","provide","access","datum","safeguard","user privacy","ensure","transparency","accountability","build","an evidence base","address","misinformation and disinformation and hate speech","inform","government","industry","policy","standard","good","practice","sdgs","call","digital","technology","company","developer","continue","develop","solution","publicly","action","counter","potential","harm","include","hate speech","discrimination","artificial","intelligence","enab